VeridianOS: TreeViewPlugin: say so when its embedded QML files are missing

Follows 0001, which resolves the module's QML files under the resource
prefix ECM gives them (":/qt/qml/org/kde/kirigamiaddons/treeview"). If a
later ECM or Qt changed that prefix, every lookup would quietly fail and
TreeViewDecoration would be registered with a URL that does not exist,
noticed only when a QML file uses it. registerTypes() now checks that the
base file is there and prints a warning naming the path otherwise. No
change while the files are where 0001 expects them.

--- a/src/treeview/treeviewplugin.cpp
+++ b/src/treeview/treeviewplugin.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,9 @@
 {
     Q_ASSERT(QLatin1String(uri) == QLatin1String("org.kde.kirigamiaddons.treeview"));
     const QString style = QQuickStyle::name();
+    if (!QFile::exists(resolveFilePath(QStringLiteral("TreeViewDecoration.qml")))) {
+        qWarning("TreeViewPlugin: %s is not in the plugin's resources", qPrintable(resolveFilePath(QStringLiteral("TreeViewDecoration.qml"))));
+    }
 
 
 #if !defined(Q_OS_ANDROID) && !defined(Q_OS_IOS)
